\section{Uniformity defined by \texorpdfstring{$d_r$}{dr}}

The family $\{d_r\}_{r>0}$ induces not only a topology but also a quasi-uniformity. Moreover, an even weaker version of the triangle inequality suffices to define the quasi-uniformity.
In particular, this weaker triangle inequality is satisfied in the space of graph embeddings $\embgraph{\mathbb{R}^N}$, as defined in \graphemb. 

