    Here $\textsf{last}$ indicates the last position of a finite trace, i.e.,  $\textsf{last}:= \neg (\ltlfX \ltlftrue)$ and $\alphabet:= 2^{\ap} = \setnocond{a:= \neg \text{good}, b:= \text{good}}$. %Observe that $\finlang{\D} \cup \finlang{\C} = \setnocond{a,b}^+$, the set of all finite traces over $\alphabet$.
