This finding is particularly significant as it extends quasipotential theory to high-dimensional networked systems with higher-order interactions, providing a unifying framework to understand the seemingly contradictory effects of these interactions: they simultaneously deepen the potential wells of non-twisted states while expanding their basins of attraction.

