%
This contrast highlights a key limitation of the current approach: while the model generalizes well across different spatial regions and temporal windows, its numerical extrapolation capability—especially for rare, high-magnitude events—is more constrained.
To better illustrate this, Figure~\ref{fig:ike_distribution} shows the water elevation distributions during the peak 12-hour window in both regions. In Corpus Christi, the surge values are well contained within the training normalization range, mostly below 2.5 meters. In Galveston Bay, however, the majority of values exceed 3 meters, with many reaching as high as 5 meters. 
