Translations were initially generated using \texttt{GPT-4o} and then rigorously reviewed by native speakers fluent in both English and the target language. This human-in-the-loop verification ensured semantic consistency, fluency, and cultural appropriateness across languages. Reviewers corrected errors, resolved ambiguous phrasing, and flagged problematic content. Consistency checks were applied across all social attributes, and representative samples were re-evaluated to validate annotation quality. This pipeline ensured that all 6,875 VQA pairs met high standards of accuracy, inclusivity, and fairness across languages and attributes.

