    To demonstrate the inefficacy of optimising long stretches of the beamline with a large optimisation problem, a test was conducted where Sequences 2-5 were combined into a single optimisation problem, involving 14 corrective steerers. Figure \ref{fig:hebt_full} illustrates the results, with the most noticeable observation being the lack of improvement over iterations. The best point reached during random sampling was never exceeded, and the final transmission from HEBT:FC0 to HEBT2:FC4 was 68\%, significantly lower than the 86\% achieved using smaller sequences. 

