\paragraph{Gaussian case:}
Beginning with the (easiest) case of Gaussian noise, we generated a
noisy version of the Sloth image shown in~\Cref{FigGauss} by choosing
$w_i \sim N(0, \sigma^2)$. Using this noisy image (represented as a
vector $y \in \real^\numobs$, with $\numobs = 512 \times 512$), we
then computed the plug-and-play estimate $\fhat_\gamma$ for a range of
smoothing parameters $\gamma$.  In the top row of~\Cref{FigGauss}, we
plot the denoised images $\fhat_\gamma$ for five different choices of
