refitting estimates are upper bounds on the true MSE once $\rho$ is
sufficiently large; in this example, setting $\rho = 1.15$ is
sufficient.

Panel (b) in~\Cref{FigGauss} compares the MSE obtained by the oracle
choice $\gamma^*$ to the MSE obtained by the wild refitting choice
$\gamwild$; in each case, we plot these MSEs versus the true standard
