\subsubsection{Group FEM for the nonlinear term}

To handle the nonlinear term $(\mathcal{N}_w, R_{i,p})$ in ~\eqref{FEMsystem_of_eqxns}, we shall use the group finite-element approach~\cite{FLETCHER1983225}. Assume that the nonlinear function $\mathcal{N}_w$ is approximated by $n$ NURBS basis functions of order $p$:
$$
  \mathcal{N}_w \approx \sum_{j=2}^{n-1} \nu_{j}(w) R_{j,p} + \sum_{j \in \{1,n\}} \nu_{j}(w) R_{j,p}.
$$
Note that the coefficients $\nu_j(w)$ still contain nonlinearity.
The nonlinear term in~\eqref{FEMsystem_of_eqxns} can be written as follows:
\begin{align}
\displaystyle (\mathcal{N}_w,R_{i,p}) =  \sum_{j=2}^{n-1} \nu_j(w) (R_{j,p},R_{i,p}) + \sum_{j \in \{1,n\}} \nu_j(w) (R_{j,p},R_{i,p}),
\end{align}
for all $i = 2,\dots,n-1$. The inner products in the above equation are computed using Gauss-Legendre quadrature rule, outlined in Section~\ref{sec:GSQ}.


